From: Enceka <enceka@yeah.net>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: connect NPU owner to PON update close

Keep a checked lifecycle owner across failed close attempts. Borrow the
published provider under flow_offload_mutex and arbitrate the shared FE
before closing GDM routes, bank1 gate and authorization. Drain only bank1
after QUIET, retaining its original registers on every retry.

An explicit claim requires idle native policy and a generation that fits
the gate ABI. PON mapping updates close an existing owner before removing
flows. Global stop retires ownership before provider teardown. Reopening
and PON qualification remain disabled until service admission is wired.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
@@ -774,6 +774,7 @@
 		bool cfg_owned;
 	} ct_ifc;
 	bool ct_host_ppe;
+	struct airoha_npu_owner *ct_npu_owner;
 	/* Set only after hardware isolates ingress source and encapsulation for
 	 * shared IP FOE keys. No runtime enable path exists yet.
 	 */
@@ -996,6 +997,8 @@
 int airoha_bank1_routes_claim(struct airoha_eth *eth, const void *owner);
 int airoha_bank1_routes_release(struct airoha_eth *eth, const void *owner);
 int airoha_ct_cpu_fallback(struct airoha_eth *eth);
+int airoha_ppe_npu_owner_claim_locked(struct airoha_eth *eth, u64 generation);
+int airoha_ppe_npu_owner_close_locked(struct airoha_eth *eth);
 int airoha_ppe_ct_shutdown(struct airoha_eth *eth);
